c327f6b030006cbe8514cb01cfb1160411e5adc","commits":[],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","finding_commits":{},"parent":"cc327f6b030006cbe8514cb01cfb1160411e5adc","patch_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","tree":"0ee85ab844c0e61de1cef3806e7c86ac8fcf4001"},"dispositions":{"comments":[{"body":"Current-span enrichment bypasses explicit instrumentation suppression. With `setAddAttributesToCurrentSpan(true)`, running GraphQL inside `InstrumentationUtil.suppressInstrumentation(...)` still writes `graphql.operation.name` and `graphql.document` onto the enclosing recording span. I reproduced this with the operation span both enabled and disabled: span creation is correctly suppressed, but enrichment is not, because the current span is captured independently of the suppression check. Honor instrumentation suppression before capturing or modifying the current span, while retaining parent-context propagation for data fetchers. A regression test should assert that a suppressed execution leaves the enclosing span untouched.","line":138,"path":"instrumentation/graphql-java/graphql-java-common-12.0/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/graphql/common/v12_0/internal/OpenTelemetryInstrumentationHelper.java","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"Exceptional completion loses all exception telemetry in current-span-only mode. With `setAddAttributesToCurrentSpan(true).setOperationSpanEnabled(false)`, an exceptionally completed `executeAsync` supplies a null result and a non-null throwable, so this branch skips the current span and `instrumenter.end` is also skipped. A failed future from a custom execution strategy reproduces a sole enclosing span with UNSET status and no exception event; enabling the operation span records ERROR and the exception on that span. Handle the throwable on the captured current span as well, without ending that enclosing span, so replacing the operation span does not discard execution failures.","line":172,"path":"instrumentation/graphql-java/graphql-java-common-12.0/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/graphql/common/v12_0/internal/OpenTelemetryInstrumentationHelper.java","side":"RIGHT"}],"input_identity":{"pr_diff_sha256":"267b15a9fc0609b57b6da03898cb4fe1e38f188bb010d8d3f4723a7d50a03caf"},"outcome":"comments","request_digest":"d61696495949443d4497c94190d0251686761db3ac0ca248eb2fdfb29d229930","schema":2},"download_sha256":"e546230eea5842103f85e5b7125e58091556e5f816f5c445575b1c238a6f3fbc","frozen_sha":"cc327f6b030006cbe8514cb01cfb1160411e5adc","pr":19177,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"d61696495949443d4497c94190d0251686761db3ac0ca248eb2fdfb29d229930","request_id":"5be12f86ccaa4f158a0a125a81b11670","run_attempt":1,"run_id":39355461690,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:e546230eea5842103f85e5b7125e58091556e5f816f5c445575b1c238a6f3fbc","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":39357657636},"workflow_revision":"1cc5e4db6ba59d691172ae66fe4a7ff3b0d1300b"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"base_ref":"main","base_sha":"fda4d07c7173131830976f0019659e070d5f4bbc","baseline_review_ids":[],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[],"frozen_at":1792460885,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-20T01:48:05Z","frozen_sha":"cc327f6b030006cbe8514cb01cfb1160411e5adc","head_ref":"feature/graphql-local-root-attributes","head_repo":"amccague/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":1242417975,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":39355417428},"loop_kind":"pr_review","merge_base_sha":"decebd668cb0f772017d785376c7910ebb9edabd","mode":"publish","pr":19177,"pr_author_id":331727,"protocol":"gi